        "treatment": "A&E treatment at Queen Elizabeth Hospital (QEH) and analgesic",
        "is_surgical": false,
        "source": [
          "Soon after the accident, he was treated in A&E Department of Queen Elizabeth Hospital (“the QEH”). He was hit by the bike handle during the accident. His general condition was good. Examination showed tenderness over chest wall. X-ray of chest and rib showed no fracture. The clinical diagnosis was chest wall injury. He was treated and discharged with analgesic. He was given 3 days sick leave (12 to 14 January 2010). Permanent disability was unlikely."
